  "step_3": "The decision reason requires: (1) identifying the reference value (zero in this case), (2) computing differences between outcomes and the reference value (i.e., the outcomes themselves), and (3) evaluating the weighted mean of these differences (i.e., expected value), and preferring the lottery with the more favorable expected value. The individual in the verbal report does not mention the reference value, nor does the individual compute or reference expected values or differences from a baseline. Instead, the individual focuses on the maximum possible gain (up to 90%) and the fact that both options involve winning. This reflects a different reasoning pattern — possibly a focus on risk or potential gain — rather than a calculation of expected differences from a reference. Since the individual does not consider the differences between outcomes and the reference value, nor apply the rule of preferring the lottery with the more favorable mean difference, the decision reason was not used. The reasoning is inconsistent with the required components of the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
